1
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:12,260
In a room planning app, a sofa is dragged 5 squares right and 2 squares down.

2
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:16,990
The app records the move as two numbers stacked in brackets.

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,720
How is that move written?

4
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:21,980
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:27,170
It is written as a column vector, with 5 on top and negative 2 underneath.

6
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:29,550
The top number is the move across.

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,970
The bottom number is the move up or down.

8
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,890
Remember: a translation slides a shape.

9
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,770
It does not turn or flip.

10
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:41,920
Move 2, 3 by 4 right and 1 up, and you get 6, 4.

11
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:45,040
A translation is described by a column vector.

12
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:50,130
The starting shape is the object, and the moved shape is the image.

13
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,590
The image is congruent to the object.

14
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:56,800
It has the same shape and size, and faces the same way.

15
00:00:56,850 --> 00:00:57,500
Your turn.

16
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:59,370
A translated image is what?

17
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:02,650
Pause the video and choose.

18
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:03,730
It is congruent.

19
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:10,410
To describe a translation, pick one vertex and count across, then up or down, to its image.

20
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:13,720
To reverse a translation, change both signs.

21
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:18,340
The reverse of 4 over negative 3 is negative 4 over 3.

22
00:01:18,390 --> 00:01:19,640
Here is the method.

23
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:21,570
Step 1: read the top number.

24
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:26,230
Move each vertex that many right, or left if it is negative.

25
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,400
Step 2: read the bottom number.

26
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:31,400
Move up, or down if it is negative.

27
00:01:31,450 --> 00:01:35,360
Step 3: plot the image vertices, and join them.

28
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:41,770
Step 4: check that the image is the same shape, the same size, and the same way round.

29
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:47,630
Translate the triangle 1, 1; 4, 1; 1, 3 by the vector negative 2 over 3.

30
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:51,750
Subtract 2 from each x, and add 3 to each y.

31
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:56,880
The image is at negative 1, 4; 2, 4; and negative 1, 6.

32
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:57,640
Your turn.

33
00:01:57,690 --> 00:02:01,900
Translate 0, 0 by the vector negative 3 over negative 4.

34
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:04,970
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:10,450
3 left and 4 down from 0, 0 gives negative 3, negative 4.

36
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:14,610
A vertex moves from 3, negative 1 to negative 2, 4.

37
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:17,950
Across: negative 2 minus 3 is negative 5.

38
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,240
Up: 4 minus negative 1 is 5.

39
00:02:20,290 --> 00:02:23,400
The vector is negative 5 over 5.

40
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:27,230
Translate by 3 over 1, then by negative 1 over 4.

41
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,480
Add the tops: 2.

42
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:29,970
Add the bottoms: 5.

43
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:34,120
It is the same as one translation by 2 over 5.

44
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:37,440
Ed translates 2, 2 by the vector 1 over 4.

45
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,570
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,720
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:42,380
He swapped the numbers.

48
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:46,820
The top number is the move across: 1 right, then 4 up.

49
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:49,850
2 plus 1 is 3, and 2 plus 4 is 6.

50
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,060
The image is 3, 6.

51
00:02:52,110 --> 00:02:55,120
Cartoon and game animators use translations.

52
00:02:55,170 --> 00:03:03,250
To move a character across the screen, the computer adds the same vector to every point, many times a second.

53
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:04,550
One last question.

54
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,510
What is the reverse of 2 over negative 5?

55
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,860
Pause the video and choose.

56
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:14,290
Change both signs: negative 2 over 5.

57
00:03:14,340 --> 00:03:20,210
To remember: in a column vector, the top is across and the bottom is up or down.

58
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:24,980
Translations keep shapes congruent, and the same way round.

59
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:28,990
Describe one by counting from a vertex to its image.

60
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,640
To reverse, change both signs.

61
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:37,030
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.3 on Camday.
